      "title": "Google cuts errors in quantum 'magic states' about 40-fold",
      "summary": "Google researchers showed on their Willow processor that a technique called magic-state cultivation reduced errors in a key quantum resource about 40-fold, and the result was published in Science. This matters because it could lower the hardware needed for error-corrected machines that do useful work. Such machines are still a long way off, and this is one building block rather than a finished computer.'",
